{"qid":"Q40","names":["Republic of Austria"],"title":"Republic of Austria","endonym":{"native":"Österreich","lang":"de"},"capsule":"The First Austrian Republic was proclaimed on 12 November 1918 from the German-speaking remnant of the Habsburg Empire after the armistice, initially styled 'German-Austria' and seeking union with Germany—a goal forbidden by the Treaty of Saint-Germain-en-Laye (1919). Chronic political polarisation between the Catholic-conservative Heimwehr and Social Democrat Schutzbund erupted into the Austrian Civil War of February 1934, after which Chancellor Engelbert Dollfuss dissolved parliament and installed an authoritarian 'Fatherland Front' regime. The republic was extinguished on 13 March 1938 when German troops crossed the border and Hitler proclaimed the Anschluss, incorporating Austria into the Third Reich.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Boundaries of the First Republic are precisely defined by the 1919 peace treaties; territorial extent is unambiguous for this period.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Britannica: Austria, history","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Austria/The-First-Republic"},{"label":"Wikipedia: First Austrian Republic","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/First_Austrian_Republic"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Anschluss","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anschluss"}],"britannica":"place/Austria","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Austria","rulers":[{"qid":"Q11726","name":"Karl Renner","start":1918,"end":1919,"image":"Karl Renner 1905.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Karl%20Renner%201905.jpg?width=320","imageLicense":{"licen